data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":8,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Range: all\nRows: 11, Columns: 2\nValues:\n[[\"Notes\", null], [\"No.\", \"Note\"], [1, \"Fill placed on the stripped and proof-rolled subgrade at El. 745.0 within the Block A slab-on-grade footprint, grids B-G / 1-5. Plan area of the pad is 11,400 sf. Each lift covered the full pad area.\"], [2, \"Subgrade proof roll performed 06/18/2026 with a loaded tandem-axle dump truck in the presence of Vantree Materials Testing. Written acceptance of the subgrade was issued by Thelbridge Project Management Services under memo TPM-26-063 dated 06/18/2026 prior to the first lift.\"], [3, \"Production test strip executed 06/19/2026 at the north end of the pad, witnessed by Vantree Materials Testing and Thelbridge Project Management Services. The strip established 6 coverage passes of the CS56B smooth-drum vibratory roller with pneumatic follow-pass at 8 in loose lift thickness as the production pattern.\"], [4, \"Structural fill for this pad was drawn from the stockpile north of Block C, approved for reuse under RFI 079 (closed 10/10/2025). Haul was by on-site scraper and articulated truck from the stockpile face; no off-site delivery tickets apply to this work.\"], [5, \"Governing laboratory Proctor carried on this record is Vantree Materials Testing Report VMT-25-0918-P04 dated 09/18/2025, ASTM D1557 Method C, \\u03b3d,max = 128.4 pcf, wopt = 9.2%, as used on the Block B mass fill record RB-FPR-BB-2025.\"], [6, \"Lift acceptance: each lift was tested by Vantree Materials Testing before the succeeding lift was placed, in accordance with Specification Section 31 20 00 Article 1.6.B. Field density reports were issued lift-by-lift as FDR-BA-01 through FDR-BA-05, three tests per lift; Lift 6 results are reported in Field Density Report SF-26-0708.\"], [7, \"Weather: no full shifts lost. Ambient temperatures ran high through the placement period and surface moisture loss between spreading and rolling was noted by the field engineer on 06/26 and 06/30.\"], [8, \"Retest and rework: interim rework passes for moisture correction and additional roller coverage are noted in the Remarks column and are covered in more detail in the daily field density reports.\"], [9, \"Distribution: original filed with Rowan Bay field engineering; copy transmitted to Thelbridge Project Management Services (Owner's Representative) and to Vantree Materials Testing for correlation with the field density reports.\"]]"}],"structuredContent":{"range":"all","values":[["Notes",null],["No.","Note"],[1,"Fill placed on the stripped and proof-rolled subgrade at El. 745.0 within the Block A slab-on-grade footprint, grids B-G / 1-5. Plan area of the pad is 11,400 sf. Each lift covered the full pad area."],[2,"Subgrade proof roll performed 06/18/2026 with a loaded tandem-axle dump truck in the presence of Vantree Materials Testing. Written acceptance of the subgrade was issued by Thelbridge Project Management Services under memo TPM-26-063 dated 06/18/2026 prior to the first lift."],[3,"Production test strip executed 06/19/2026 at the north end of the pad, witnessed by Vantree Materials Testing and Thelbridge Project Management Services. The strip established 6 coverage passes of the CS56B smooth-drum vibratory roller with pneumatic follow-pass at 8 in loose lift thickness as the production pattern."],[4,"Structural fill for this pad was drawn from the stockpile north of Block C, approved for reuse under RFI 079 (closed 10/10/2025). Haul was by on-site scraper and articulated truck from the stockpile face; no off-site delivery tickets apply to this work."],[5,"Governing laboratory Proctor carried on this record is Vantree Materials Testing Report VMT-25-0918-P04 dated 09/18/2025, ASTM D1557 Method C, γd,max = 128.4 pcf, wopt = 9.2%, as used on the Block B mass fill record RB-FPR-BB-2025."],[6,"Lift acceptance: each lift was tested by Vantree Materials Testing before the succeeding lift was placed, in accordance with Specification Section 31 20 00 Article 1.6.B. Field density reports were issued lift-by-lift as FDR-BA-01 through FDR-BA-05, three tests per lift; Lift 6 results are reported in Field Density Report SF-26-0708."],[7,"Weather: no full shifts lost. Ambient temperatures ran high through the placement period and surface moisture loss between spreading and rolling was noted by the field engineer on 06/26 and 06/30."],[8,"Retest and rework: interim rework passes for moisture correction and additional roller coverage are noted in the Remarks column and are covered in more detail in the daily field density reports."],[9,"Distribution: original filed with Rowan Bay field engineering; copy transmitted to Thelbridge Project Management Services (Owner's Representative) and to Vantree Materials Testing for correlation with the field density reports."]]},"isError":false}}

